RISC3D test kit 30 (prototype, 15 November 2026)
================================================

Kit 29's results: Linux's own Mesa on the Pi draws TORCS's lighting
wrongly too (LitLinuxPicture = LitPicture). So it's a bug in the Pi's
Mesa (V3D, 25.0.7): with GL_LIGHTING on, textures lose their
coordinates. It isn't specular, emission or colour material.

This kit draws twelve variations of the lit plane with Linux's Mesa
directly, to find one the bug doesn't touch, so that rol-3d can draw
TORCS that way:

  row 1: as before (wrong) | unlit (right) | glBegin/glEnd | arrays in a VBO
  row 2: 4-component texture coordinates | GL_LIGHT0 off | local viewer |
         two-sided lighting
  row 3: separate specular colour | texture matrix not identity |
         generated texture coordinates | flat shading

It runs three times: the GPU as normal, the GPU with Mesa told to give
OpenGL 2.1 instead of 3.1, and software (all right).

Nothing to install (keep riscos-risc3d 0.17-1).

Steps
-----
 1. Unzip RISC3DTest into HardDisc4, replacing kit 29.
 2. In RiSH's Root shell:
      sh /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/litx

